# The aLLManac — the LATEST channel.  Image pins, nothing else.
# =============================================================================
# The dev playground's pins.  See channels/stable.env for what a channel is.
# The rule for this file: a pin moves here FIRST, gets deployed to a box
# nobody teaches on, gets walked, and only then moves to stable.  What is
# here and not in stable is exactly the upgrade under test — keep the
# comment on each line saying what is being validated and since when.
#
# Still pinned, not `latest`: a moving tag would make "what broke?"
# unanswerable, and the answer is the whole point of the channel.
# =============================================================================

# Under test since 2026-09-15: 0.8.8-rc3.  What we are watching for — the
# Agent Management API with M2M auth (the seeder's forged JWT should go), the
# footer emitted with the HTML shell (the CUSTOM_FOOTER wall), OpenID
# discovery retries, the interface schema (the lockdown keys), memory as an
# agent capability, the design-system refactor vs. the branding asset mounts.
LIBRECHAT_IMAGE=ghcr.io/danny-avila/librechat:v0.8.8-rc3
